WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.702
-Hey, guys, as I mentioned
earlier in the week,

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.137
tonight we are kicking off
our annual "Tonight Show"

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.705
Book Club Summer Reads.

00:00:06.705 --> 00:00:09.675
Very excited about this.
Here's how it works.

00:00:09.675 --> 00:00:11.744
I picked out six books.
-Six.

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.280
-And I'm going to read
one of them.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.682
-Now?

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.317
-No, but I've --
I'm not sure which one.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:19.852
They all look good.
I know about them.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:21.287
I've done research
on all of them.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:22.788
I'm going to tell you
about each one,

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:24.523
and then you guys
are going to vote on which book

00:00:24.523 --> 00:00:26.459
should be this year's
Summer Read,

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.527
and we can all read it together.

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:29.795
-Ah.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.364
-So now it's time
to reveal the books.

00:00:32.364 --> 00:00:33.699
Here we go. All right.

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:36.836
Here's our first book
right here.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.271
"People We Meet on Vacation."

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:40.106
-Ooh.
-I like the cover, right?

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.975
You like the cover?
Now, it's by Emily Henry.

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:45.077
This is a "New York Times"
best-selling author.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.946
This is a fun romance.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.114
-Ooh. Romance?
-Yeah, it's romance.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.649
So here's the deal
with this one.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.952
It's about two friends --
Poppy and her best friend, Alex.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.221
All right? A man and woman.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.290
They go on vacation together
every year.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.058
Except last year.
There was some drama.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:00.593
So they didn't go.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.429
They didn't go on vacation.
-Ooh. COVID?

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:04.164
-But now they want
to go on vacation.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:08.167
No, no, it wasn't the --
It was a different drama.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:11.938
Now they want to go on vacation
one last time to fix everything.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.007
But then the question
is brought up,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:17.276
can men and women
ever be just friends?

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:19.812
-Ooh.
I'll have what she's having.

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.347
-It's like a -- Yeah.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.216
It's a "Harry Met Sally"
type of thing.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.917
Emily Henry.
"People We Meet on Vacation."

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.586
That's book one.
-Okay. Book one.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.021
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:32.392
-All right. Ready for this one?

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.694
"Razorblade Tears."
-Ooh!

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.996
-By S.A. Cosby.
-Sss!

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:40.500
-Yeah. His last novel,
"Blacktop Wasteland,"

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.303
won "L.A. Times'" Book Award
for Best Mystery.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.737
-Ooh.

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.539
-A good summer read.
You want a murder mystery.

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:47.973
Right?
So this is a murder mystery.

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:51.110
Takes place in the South.
It's about two ex-convicts.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.678
Their sons are murdered,

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:54.848
but the local cops
won't do anything about it.

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.448
-Ohh.

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:59.586
-So now they have to take
matters into their own hands.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.521
Story of retribution
and redemption.

00:02:02.521 --> 00:02:04.757
-This is Alex and Poppy?
-[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.026
-No, no. Alex and Poppy --

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.528
No, this is two ex-convicts
in this one.

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.430
I don't know --
Again, I have not read them.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.033
Alex and Poppy --
they could be the ex-convicts,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.168
but it's not in the description
of the book.

00:02:16.168 --> 00:02:18.671
-"Razorblade Tears."
-"Razorblade Tears."

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.506
There you go.
That's your mystery.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:21.975
That's your second choice.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.376
All right. Here's one.
Ready for this one?

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.345
-I'm ready.
[ Imitates whip crack ]

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:28.414
-"One Last Stop."
-Ooh.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:31.751
-Casey McQuiston.
-I like that name. McQuiston.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.619
-Any guess what this is about,
by the cover?

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.955
-I think it's about someone
who goes to Purpleville,

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.024
and there's a stop on the train,

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.426
but they have to stop
one last time.

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.095
'Cause they have to go
to the restroom.

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:44.097
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.431
Close?

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.033
-Tariq, you have any guesses
what this book's about,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.234
by the cover?

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.668
-Um, I'm going to guess --
Okay.

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:52.438
Somebody hops on a flight.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:56.442
Um, the plane is redirected
because the fuel issues.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:03:00.480
They have to land
in some remote area to refuel.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:03.616
-You're getting that
from this cover?

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:04.951
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.652
-[ Laughter ]
-The subway.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:09.288
-And there's something wrong
with the jet fuel. Yeah.

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:11.690
-Potay-toe, potah-toe, man.
-No, it's a subway train.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.393
-Oh, subway.
-It's a subway train.

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:17.196
All right. Ready for this?
So, Casey --

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.931
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:20.333
Casey McQuiston.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.034
"New York Times"
best-selling author.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.971
This is another romance.
-Ooh. Romance.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:27.406
People -- It's the summertime.
You want the murder mystery

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.074
